--- !u!114 &2075258879
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2075258877}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 31d97d943f616874496536519f0de0c7, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TD_Game.ContextTutorial
  panel: {fileID: 2075258880}
  text: {fileID: 1948657171}
  secondsPerHint: 5
  fadeTime: 0.25
  battlePosition: {x: -120, y: 62}
  startHint: "{Move} move   \xB7   {Sprint} sprint   \xB7   {Jump} jump\nLand on
    an enemy from a jump to AMBUSH it."
  battleControlsHint: "{Attack} attack   \xB7   {Skill1} {Skill2} skills   \xB7  
    {Potion} potion   \xB7   {Ultimate} Tonalli Burst   \xB7   {Artifact} artifact  
    \xB7   {EndTurn} end turn\nWhile attacking, press {Attack} again right before
    the blow for a CRITICAL. {Target} (or click an enemy) chooses the target."
  quickTimeDodgeHint: 'The enemy glows red before it strikes.

    Press {Dodge}
    right before the hit: no damage and a counter-attack. Too early = the button
    locks.'
  quickTimeInterruptHint: 'Spells cannot be dodged: INTERRUPT them.

    Press {Interrupt}
    right before the spell is cast.'
  orbsHint: "Walk over the orbs before leaving:\ngold = Macuahuitl charge   \xB7  
    green = life   \xB7   blue = Tonalli"
  unlockHint: You learned a new skill. Use it in battle with {Skill1} or {Skill2}.
  backToStartHint: 'When you fall, you go back to the BEGINNING of the map.

    You
    keep your skills, gold and growth, and you always get potions to retry.'
  secondsBetweenTips: 25
  explorationTips:
  - "Press {Map} to open the map of Mictl\xE1n: enemies, merchants, villagers and
    side quests are marked on it."
  - Villagers with a gold ! over their heads have something new to tell. Talk to
    them with {Interact}.
  - Rivers and ravines are dangerous. Jump ({Jump}) over the narrow parts; sprint
    ({Sprint}) first to jump farther.
  - Fallen logs, bushes and low rocks can be jumped over. Look for shortcuts.
  - 'A merchant waits in every region. Gold is scarce: choose well.'
  - Enemies Left (bottom right) counts the servants of the gods still standing. When
    it reaches 0, the obsidian key appears.
  - Press {Pause} to pause the game and change the volume.
